---
import { site } from "../../config/site";
import PlaceholderImage from "../PlaceholderImage.astro";
---

<section id="about" class="border-t border-line py-16 md:py-24">
  <div
    class="fade-in-section mx-auto grid max-w-[1100px] items-start gap-10 px-4 sm:px-6 md:grid-cols-[5fr_7fr] md:gap-14"
  >
    <PlaceholderImage
      alt={`${site.advisor.fullName} at work as a business broker`}
      ratio="4 / 5"
      class="max-w-[320px] justify-self-center md:max-w-none md:justify-self-start"
    />

    <div>
      <h2
        class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-4xl"
      >
        About {site.advisor.name}
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-6 flex max-w-prose flex-col gap-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        <p>
          I'm a licensed business broker in Minneapolis. I work on the sell
          side, which means I spend my days valuing small businesses, listing
          them, qualifying buyers, comparing offers, and getting deals to
          close. <span class="placeholder-value">{site.proof.dealsWorked}</span>
          deals in, I've seen most of the ways a first-time buyer gets hurt,
          and almost all of them were avoidable.
        </p>
        <p>
          I started this because of the messages I get on TikTok. People who
          want to buy a business, have the money and the work ethic, and have
          no idea how the process actually works or who to trust. The options
          available to them were either a $15,000 program or a $150,000
          advisor, and most of what those charge for is finding deals. There
          are plenty of deals. What buyers need is someone who knows what
          they're looking at.
        </p>
        <p>
          So this is that. I don't find deals, I don't run diligence, and I
          don't take a cut. I sit next to you, tell you what I'd do, and keep
          you from spending money in the wrong order.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-ink-soft">
        Licensed in Minnesota. Advisory clients anywhere in the US.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
